;; A specification and interface vocabulary only. There is NO seed AST.
((version . 1)
 (goal . "Build an entire Scheme program from an empty AST, targeting Chibi Scheme and its native R7RS-small runtime. Generate every import, definition, helper, and function body. Export by top-level definition two procedures: (run-r7rs text) and (main arguments). run-r7rs executes every datum in the supplied string in order, with definitions and imports persisting between calls in a guest environment; it returns the program's captured stdout as a string. Do not print expression values automatically. Handle empty input, hygienic macros, define-library, guest eval, and errors; propagate errors and close owned ports, also on exceptional exit. main implements no arguments = read a program from stdin; (\"--eval\" SOURCE) = run SOURCE; one filename = read and run that file. main displays explicit program output and rejects invalid arguments. Do not invoke main at top level: the external launcher only loads your complete generated program and invokes main. Chibi provides R7RS libraries including (scheme eval), (scheme read), (scheme write), (scheme file), (scheme process-context); (chibi io) optionally provides port->string. eval takes an expression AND environment. You choose and implement all control flow. Use the smallest correct implementation. No interpreter template or solution fragments are supplied.")
 (runtime . "Chibi Scheme 0.12, native R7RS-small. Every candidate must provide its own imports. eval accepts a datum and an environment. Chibi's (meta) environment supplies library-declaration forms, distinct from ordinary expression evaluation. Its mutable-environment creates a mutable environment from import specifications. resolve-import maps a specification to (module-name . bindings); load-module loads a module; module-env extracts its environment; %import accepts target environment, source environment, bindings, and immutable? flag. These native facilities support imports into an explicit guest environment. Capture host read/eval bindings so guest definitions cannot replace the interpreter's reader/evaluator. Argument evaluation order is unspecified. Generate all control flow yourself.")
 (symbols run-r7rs main)
 (literals "--eval"))
